<node id="Mission-Critical Workload">
  <data key="d0">Mission-Critical Workload</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mission-Critical Workload refers to an application or workload where failure has severe business consequences, requiring the highest levels of reliability, availability, resiliency, and fault tolerance. These workloads must be available continuously—all day, every day—demanding zero-downtime deployments and highly available operations. They are typically significant in scale and complexity, generating high volumes of operational data.

In the context of Microsoft Azure, mission-critical workloads often employ globally distributed, active-active, multi-region deployment designs to maximize resilience. They require effective operational procedures and adherence to operational best practices. Mission-critical workloads form the basis of the Azure Well-Architected series on data platform design, emphasizing principles of high availability, fault tolerance, and reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;A mission-critical workload is a collection of application resources that must be highly reliable, always available, resilient to failures, and operational on the platform.&lt;SEP&gt;A mission-critical workload is a type of workload described in the Well-Architected framework requiring high reliability and security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7092b7ad42e474e7a19995579b487a34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-682b99a48c23e193c28d8a4eae469e68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a324803e46dec295e5d9abb5a43f8a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65bdd00b5709152c19e73a1ad56171cd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-assessment.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scale-Unit Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Scale-Unit Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Scale-unit architecture is a design pattern that optimizes end-to-end scalability through compartmentalization, allowing logical units to be scaled independently.&lt;SEP&gt;Scale-unit architecture is a design pattern for distributing resources across Azure regions as part of deployment stamps.&lt;SEP&gt;Scale-unit architecture is a design pattern for mission-critical application deployment and scaling.&lt;SEP&gt;A key architectural practice for achieving zero-downtime deployments in mission-critical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Scale-unit architecture is an application design pattern referenced in the mission-critical architecture documentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11bac6534273a4d1656750c49ac2fcee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291484</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scale Unit">
  <data key="d0">Scale Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A scale unit is a logical unit or function that can be scaled independently, comprising code components, hosting platforms, deployment stamps, and subscriptions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290812</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deployment Stamp">
  <data key="d0">Deployment Stamp</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment stamp is a pattern that covers related components and can be deployed as a regional unit to horizontally scale a solution.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment stamp is a regional resource deployment that typically corresponds to a scale unit.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment stamp contains both infrastructure and application layers, treated as ephemeral with a lifecycle tied to a single release.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment stamp is a regional deployment unit placed in a dedicated subscription so subscription limits apply only within that stamp's context.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment stamp is an independent regional deployment unit that can be constrained to a single zone or spread across zones for redundancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5df507c6d7ae6d803dce8c99d84eb9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Well-Architected Framework">
  <data key="d0">Azure Well-Architected Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Well-Architected Framework is a Microsoft guidance framework providing prescriptive architecture best practices for designing, building, and operating high-quality workloads on Microsoft Azure, including mission-critical workloads. It is organized around five core pillars: Reliability (resiliency), Security, Cost Optimization, Operational Excellence, and Performance Efficiency.

The framework is structured in a layered approach consisting of pillars, workload guidance, service guides, and design guides, offering actionable architectural decisions and pillar-specific recommendations. It provides comprehensive, cross-pillar design guidance covering application design, platform considerations, scalability, and DevOps practices, along with maturity models and review assessments.

The Azure Well-Architected Framework serves as a set of guiding tenets and principles aimed at driving architectural excellence and improving the overall quality of workloads at the fundamental architectural level.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ffc0561a80ee1b478b5e827cc0c1a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11bac6534273a4d1656750c49ac2fcee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75881c2e5d7a1909b7080e2819bc0413&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb446ff77685d5a057445825bab9dcd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-682b99a48c23e193c28d8a4eae469e68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a324803e46dec295e5d9abb5a43f8a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c80c2e3daca343330a4078ee96575423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5edbb96d862689f4578c3260e170ce09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174d80fe9b4a084487aca3f0463ecf9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-387611e470f83bbe5d875c098db01fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3794cb2593672d7e205ce2c3021b80ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab2911837499c055b346ca8d6a1cac17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c445903885a1763cd6ad5557106d024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e1b9f43effe85bb4f106ab0a823c7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4e1326f308873031b3e530e46d8478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180631bfef52e56155ab10e925a1d9c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d07c7fd7e0ea2028615959913f9c73</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/pillars.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/what-is-well-architected-framework.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/workloads.md</data>
