</node>
<node id="Autoscaling">
  <data key="d0">Autoscaling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoscaling is the practice of automatically adjusting resource capacity in response to load changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscaling is configured based on service-internal and application-set thresholds to respond to load-level volatility.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscaling is the Azure-native capability to automatically scale services based on demand, prioritized for services that support it.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292095</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global Distribution">
  <data key="d0">Global Distribution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Global distribution is a strategy for deploying applications across multiple regions in an active/active model to withstand regional and zone failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Global distribution is an application design pattern for deploying across multiple regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290968</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capacity Model">
  <data key="d0">Capacity Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A capacity model defines the scope and relationships between scale units based on performance and non-functional requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;A capacity model is used to monitor data volume, scale limits, and expected growth rates.&lt;SEP&gt;A model enabling planning of resource scale levels for a given load profile and system-wide capacity allocation planning.&lt;SEP&gt;A capacity model quantifies scale relationships between components to ensure automated scale operations encompass all related components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4678f659d2199619f053d40287ff2e4a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AKS">
  <data key="d0">AKS</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">AKS (Azure Kubernetes Service) is a managed Kubernetes container orchestration platform on Azure that supports cluster and node management, upgrades, networking, monitoring, and governance. It has scale limits such as 1,000 nodes per cluster and has a hard requirement for an underlying virtual network, requiring network integration configuration with support for Azure CNI and Kubenet networking plugins.

AKS serves as a primary application platform where health endpoints can be configured for pods, and it is monitored for CPU utilization and deployment statuses. It can also be used as a compute platform with services such as Azure Cosmos DB for query-intensive workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d7d8989458b7b6a8098b2c4cc007937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noisy Neighbor Antipattern">
  <data key="d0">Noisy Neighbor Antipattern</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Noisy Neighbor antipattern occurs when shared resources are consumed disproportionately, and can be avoided by dedicating landing zone subscriptions to specific applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290814</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Landing Zone">
  <data key="d0">Azure Landing Zone</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Landing Zone is a foundational platform architecture pattern and pre-configured deployment environment in Azure for deploying applications and resources. It provides Azure policies ensuring consistent reliability and security, and recommends dedicated subscriptions for mission-critical workloads.

Azure Landing Zone offers Online and Corp. Connected variants for different network configurations, providing connectivity to on-premises networks using ExpressRoute or virtual network designs. It serves as a deployment context for integrating with broader organizational network topology following Microsoft best practices.

The architecture supports centralized storage of operational data, allowing data to be forked into both centralized tooling and application-dedicated Log Analytics workspaces. A central platform Log Analytics workspace may need to be queried for platform resource dependencies.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure landing zone provides an additional threat mitigation layer through centralized security capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure landing zone is a deployment environment that provides network connectivity to on-premises data centers.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Landing Zone is an environment with centralized baseline policy assignments applied at management group and subscription levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5df507c6d7ae6d803dce8c99d84eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c9347a4bec9630cfbf008260182d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc6c19c90a7ec75e7d95d807c1817fcf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active/Active Model">
  <data key="d0">Active/Active Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An active/active deployment strategy that maximizes availability and provides a higher composite SLA by distributing load among all regions.&lt;SEP&gt;The active/active model is a deployment approach where load is distributed among all regions to maximize resilience against regional failures.&lt;SEP&gt;The active/active model is a multi-region deployment strategy strongly recommended for mission-critical workloads where multiple regions run simultaneously.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290966</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id=".NET SDK">
  <data key="d0">.NET SDK</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The .NET SDK is a software development kit for Azure that provides more capabilities and is updated frequently, prioritized for reliability and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ffc0561a80ee1b478b5e827cc0c1a93</data>
