<node id="Circuit Breaker">
  <data key="d0">Circuit Breaker</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern used to implement resiliency in application code for handling failures.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern that provides stability by waiting for recovery or quickly rejecting requests rather than blocking while waiting for unavailable remote services.&lt;SEP&gt;Circuit Breaker is a software engineering pattern used to implement resilient applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ffc0561a80ee1b478b5e827cc0c1a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36d66c785cc9b10b4cf377888b6bd59f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290815</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Queue-Based Load Leveling">
  <data key="d0">Queue-Based Load Leveling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern that introduces a buffer between consumers and requested resources to ensure consistent load levels through queued requests processed by worker processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Queue-Based Load Leveling is a software engineering pattern for managing load in cloud applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ffc0561a80ee1b478b5e827cc0c1a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36d66c785cc9b10b4cf377888b6bd59f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290815</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retry">
  <data key="d0">Retry</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern that handles transient failures elegantly through cancel, immediate retry, or retry after delay strategies with suitable back-off.&lt;SEP&gt;Retry is a software engineering pattern for handling transient failures in applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ffc0561a80ee1b478b5e827cc0c1a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36d66c785cc9b10b4cf377888b6bd59f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290815</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bulkhead">
  <data key="d0">Bulkhead</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern that partitions service instances into groups based on load and availability requirements, isolating failures to sustain service functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulkhead is a software engineering pattern for isolating application components to prevent cascading failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ffc0561a80ee1b478b5e827cc0c1a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36d66c785cc9b10b4cf377888b6bd59f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290815</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Saga">
  <data key="d0">Saga</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern that manages data consistency across microservices with independent datastores through defined event or message channels and compensating transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Saga is a software engineering pattern for managing distributed transactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ffc0561a80ee1b478b5e827cc0c1a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36d66c785cc9b10b4cf377888b6bd59f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290815</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Throttling">
  <data key="d0">Throttling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern that controls resource consumption by deferring lower-priority operations when a resource reaches a load threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;Throttling is a software engineering pattern for controlling resource consumption in applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ffc0561a80ee1b478b5e827cc0c1a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36d66c785cc9b10b4cf377888b6bd59f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290816</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Endpoint Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Health Endpoint Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern that implements functional checks in an application accessible through exposed endpoints at regular intervals to inform application health.&lt;SEP&gt;Health Endpoint Monitoring is a pattern for checking the health of application services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ffc0561a80ee1b478b5e827cc0c1a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36d66c785cc9b10b4cf377888b6bd59f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290816</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event-Driven Design">
  <data key="d0">Event-Driven Design</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A design approach using asynchronous message processing through an intermediary to build resiliency and support loose coupling.&lt;SEP&gt;Event-driven design is an architecture style referenced for mission-critical application design.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ffc0561a80ee1b478b5e827cc0c1a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290816</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distributed Tracing">
  <data key="d0">Distributed Tracing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A diagnostic technique for end-to-end tracing of requests across services, providing correlation IDs for error messages.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributed tracing is a diagnostic method for tracking requests across microservices.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributed Tracing is a diagnostic concept for tracking requests across distributed systems using correlation IDs.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributed Tracing is facilitated by Application Insights to provide comprehensive error messages with correlation IDs.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributed Tracing is a diagnostic concept for tracking requests across distributed system components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ffc0561a80ee1b478b5e827cc0c1a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7620929405aff597a8fb7046b3e2aa5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Insights">
  <data key="d0">Application Insights</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Application Insights is a feature of Azure Monitor that provides application performance monitoring (APM) and distributed tracing capabilities. It serves as a tool for querying, correlating, and visualizing application traces and telemetry data, offering deep insights into application performance.

Application Insights is an Azure Monitor resource that must be deployed and configured to incorporate data collection and querying capabilities. It can be deployed in a workspace-based model underpinned by a Log Analytics workspace. The tool facilitates distributed tracing, telemetry correlation, and provides comprehensive error messages with correlation IDs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ffc0561a80ee1b478b5e827cc0c1a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee778ccfa3886c52f485cafeef0009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7255c274585b0f1f482e338bbc6c26aa</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291792</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deployment Stamps">
  <data key="d0">Deployment Stamps</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Deployment stamps is an architecture pattern for deploying multiple independent copies of application components.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployment stamps are regional scale units used to distribute workloads across regions or within a single region for fault tolerance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ffc0561a80ee1b478b5e827cc0c1a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290963</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Availability Zones">
  <data key="d0">Availability Zones</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Availability Zones are physically separate locations within an Azure region, each typically corresponding to distinct datacenters. They provide datacenter-level fault tolerance and high availability by distributing resources—such as VMs, AKS control plane and agent nodes, and database replicas—across these separated facilities. The latency between zones is maintained at less than 2 milliseconds.

By spreading workloads across multiple zones, Availability Zones maximize resilience and reliability within a region, ensuring that a failure in one datacenter does not affect resources in another. They offer zone redundancy for services such as Azure Cosmos DB, protecting deployments against zone-level failures while keeping data and compute resources within the same region for low-latency access.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure zones within Azure regions used to distribute solution components for fault tolerance.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability Zones are Azure infrastructure zones that enable 99.99% SLA when Azure Standard Load Balancer is deployed across them.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability Zones are a reliability convention that can be enforced through Azure Policy.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability Zones are used to ensure reliable intra-region deployment configurations for Azure services.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability zones are infrastructure deployments within regions used for reliability, cost, and performance of workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca497cb3fcd5030cdda335c35addc590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3d8041b90240539202a251be26880b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c9347a4bec9630cfbf008260182d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5edbb96d862689f4578c3260e170ce09</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292438</data>
