<node id="Health Model">
  <data key="d0">Health Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A model that takes corrective action for non-transient failures that cannot be fully mitigated in application logic, informed by application instrumentation and logging.&lt;SEP&gt;A health model defines healthy and unhealthy states for each component to enable fast failure detection and recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;A model used to quantify application health, understand operational efficiency, and identify active threats.&lt;SEP&gt;A health model is an iterative construct used to define and calculate application health through aggregation of resource-level metrics, used in CI/CD pipelines and for SLO attainment.&lt;SEP&gt;The health model is a representation of application health using health probes, structured logging, and visualization with traffic light states.&lt;SEP&gt;The health model is informed by operational data and application instrumentation to facilitate predictive action and troubleshooting.&lt;SEP&gt;A health model represents application health through layered scoring functions, used to drive dashboards and alert rules.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-390c92e4b952c987f9e0e7d0deeafa36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75881c2e5d7a1909b7080e2819bc0413&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee778ccfa3886c52f485cafeef0009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291768</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
