<node id="Azure Functions">
  <data key="d0">Azure Functions</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Functions is a serverless compute platform where application logic runs as distinct functions in response to events.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Functions is a serverless compute service that provides event-driven execution with multiple hosting options.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Functions is a service that can bind to the Azure Cosmos DB change feed to process items into storage for custom backups.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Functions is a serverless compute service on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure's serverless compute service.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca497cb3fcd5030cdda335c35addc590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20168b92f579ebd286ed6e8413a80537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180631bfef52e56155ab10e925a1d9c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292779</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Logic Apps">
  <data key="d0">Azure Logic Apps</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Logic Apps is a serverless platform for creating automated workflows using a graphical user interface with built-in triggers.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Logic Apps is a cloud service for automating workflows with multiple deployment modes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca497cb3fcd5030cdda335c35addc590</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure API Management">
  <data key="d0">Azure API Management</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure API Management is an Azure service for publishing, securing, transforming, and monitoring APIs. It functions as an API gateway and management platform, enabling organizations to expose APIs to external clients and different application teams. It is relevant to mission-critical application ingress as an application delivery service. The service offers multiple tiers, including the Consumption tier and Premium v2 tier, and provides architecture best practices with refactored guidance for improved clarity and usability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca497cb3fcd5030cdda335c35addc590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ee1b46c13062b2f84bc4bd8740f6c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062b3d27f8d0d9d1409bb3878692b58b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20168b92f579ebd286ed6e8413a80537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180631bfef52e56155ab10e925a1d9c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292767</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power Apps">
  <data key="d0">Power Apps</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Power Apps provides a low-code/no-code development experience with workflow logic configurable through a user interface.&lt;SEP&gt;Power Apps is a low-code platform for building business applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca497cb3fcd5030cdda335c35addc590</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power Automate">
  <data key="d0">Power Automate</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Power Automate provides low-code/no-code workflow automation with integrations configurable through connections.&lt;SEP&gt;Power Automate is a service for automating workflows across applications and services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca497cb3fcd5030cdda335c35addc590</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Entra">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Entra</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Entra provides authentication for Azure Container Registry.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra provides integrated authentication for pushing and pulling container images.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra provides identity and role-based access control (RBAC) for Azure Cosmos DB authentication and resource management.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra provides authentication to connect to services without using connection strings or keys.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra provides custom roles used to limit authorization for permanently deleting secrets, keys, and certificates in Key Vault.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra provides activity logs that can be exported to Log Analytics Workspace for monitoring and retention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c9347a4bec9630cfbf008260182d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Premium Plan">
  <data key="d0">Premium Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Premium plan is a recommended Azure Functions hosting option that allows configuring compute instance size for maximizing reliability and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290961</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serverless Computing">
  <data key="d0">Serverless Computing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Serverless computing provides resources on demand, eliminating infrastructure management, with automatic provisioning and scaling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290961</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Image Locking">
  <data key="d0">Image Locking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Image locking prevents changes or deletions to container image versions or repositories in Container Registry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290961</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zone Redundancy">
  <data key="d0">Zone Redundancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Zone redundancy in the Premium Container Registry tier provides protection against availability zone failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290961</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Virtual Machines">
  <data key="d0">Azure Virtual Machines</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Virtual Machines serve as the primary IaaS application hosting model for constrained migrations from on-premises deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Virtual Machines are IaaS VMs provided by Azure for application hosting, requiring management of operating systems and software packages.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Virtual Machines and scale sets have updated architecture best practices reflecting new Azure features.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure's compute service for virtual machines and scale sets.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Virtual Machines and Scale Sets are compute services with architecture best practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3d8041b90240539202a251be26880b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180631bfef52e56155ab10e925a1d9c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292723</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Private Endpoints">
  <data key="d0">Private Endpoints</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Private endpoints restrict access to private virtual networks and help prevent unauthorized access, mitigating data exfiltration risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Private Endpoints provide private connectivity to Azure platform services within a virtual network.&lt;SEP&gt;Private Endpoints are a security convention enforced via Azure Policy, used to connect to services like Azure Key Vault.&lt;SEP&gt;Private Endpoints are a security convention that can be enforced through Azure Policy.&lt;SEP&gt;Private endpoints provide private connectivity to Azure services as part of Azure Private Link.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c9347a4bec9630cfbf008260182d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65bdd00b5709152c19e73a1ad56171cd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Web Application Firewall">
  <data key="d0">Web Application Firewall</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A web application firewall (WAF) provides protection for HTTP endpoints from common external attack vectors when using Azure Functions HTTP triggers.&lt;SEP&gt;Web Application Firewall (WAF) provides protection from common web exploits and vulnerabilities such as SQL injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Web Application Firewall provides protection against common web exploits such as SQL injection and cross-site scripting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ee1b46c13062b2f84bc4bd8740f6c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dedicated Plan">
  <data key="d0">Dedicated Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Dedicated plan is the least serverless Azure Functions hosting option, providing autoscale but with slower scale operations than other plans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290961</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure App Service">
  <data key="d0">Azure App Service</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure App Service is a cloud platform service provided by Microsoft Azure for hosting web applications, APIs, and containerized workloads. It serves as a low-friction container platform and an alternative to Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS), offering similar capabilities without the complexity of Kubernetes management.

Azure App Service includes features such as Auto Heal, Health Check, and availability zone configuration. Health Checks support scale-out operations and enable recycling of unhealthy instances. The platform provides secondary deployment slots that can be swapped after a deployment, facilitating zero-downtime releases.

Azure App Service operates as a multitenant environment with a limited number of outbound ports available per instance. It also has IPv6 support considerations and established architecture best practices for optimal use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca497cb3fcd5030cdda335c35addc590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50bf24a002558d213cd02700a64f5c07</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292786</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Container Registry">
  <data key="d0">Azure Container Registry</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Container Registry is a service for storing and managing container images with geo-replication and vulnerability scanning capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Container Registry is a native Azure service for hosting container images, supporting geo-replication, Microsoft Entra authentication, and automated container building.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Container Registry is an Azure service for storing and managing container images.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Container Registry is a service for storing and managing container images, supporting geo-replication, zone redundancy, private endpoints, and image locking.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Container Registry is a container image registry where old image versions should be automatically purged.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Container Registry is an Azure service that stores container images, supporting auto-purge of old versions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca497cb3fcd5030cdda335c35addc590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-682b99a48c23e193c28d8a4eae469e68</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292095</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets">
  <data key="d0">Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets provide automatic scaling, health monitoring, and automatic repair of unhealthy instances.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets enable deployment and management of groups of VMs with features like automatic instance repairs, flexible orchestration, and fault domain management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca497cb3fcd5030cdda335c35addc590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3d8041b90240539202a251be26880b7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290962</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft is the technology company that provides the Azure cloud platform and its related services. It offers Azure-native toolsets, including GitHub Actions and Azure Pipelines, for deploying and managing mission-critical applications. Microsoft operates the backbone network over which Azure Front Door forwards requests and maintains Azure IP Ranges and Service Tags. The company also provides the Zero Trust security model and Entra identity services. Microsoft continues to invest in future platform capabilities across the Azure ecosystem.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft is the organization behind Azure and the Well-Architected Framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft offers the Azure Well-Architected Review and the Well-Architected Framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca497cb3fcd5030cdda335c35addc590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ecbdde6d262012ebbdfa789102231a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65bdd00b5709152c19e73a1ad56171cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174d80fe9b4a084487aca3f0463ecf9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5505883d3947b5183a0241244e460f5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/pillars.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/what-is-well-architected-framework.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292527</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Heal">
  <data key="d0">Auto Heal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto Heal automatically recycles unhealthy workers to enable self-healing for mission-critical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Heal is a feature for Azure App Service Linux that automatically mitigates issues by recycling instances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca497cb3fcd5030cdda335c35addc590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290962</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Check">
  <data key="d0">Health Check</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Health Check identifies non-responsive workers by assessing critical downstream dependencies.&lt;SEP&gt;Health Check is a feature for monitoring App Service instances' health status.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca497cb3fcd5030cdda335c35addc590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290962</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Geo-Replication">
  <data key="d0">Geo-Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Geo-replication is a method to replicate container images across all regions in Azure Container Registry.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-replication is a capability of Azure Container Registry that replicates images to multiple regions, providing resiliency against regional outages and reducing latency.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-replication is a Container Registry feature for replicating container images across multiple Azure regions for high availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-replication is a method for deploying cache instances across different Azure regions in active-active configuration to maximize availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca497cb3fcd5030cdda335c35addc590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="App Service Plan">
  <data key="d0">App Service Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An App Service plan defines the set of compute resources for App Service, with configurable scaling rules, instance limits, and availability zone support.&lt;SEP&gt;App Service Plan defines the compute resources and scaling for apps hosted in Azure App Service.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca497cb3fcd5030cdda335c35addc590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290962</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Entra ID">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Entra ID</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Entra ID is Microsoft's identity platform that serves as a global, shared foundational service and a platform dependency for almost all Azure services. It provides centralized identity management, authentication, and authorization capabilities, offering an alternative to connection strings and keys for securing access to Azure resources.

Microsoft Entra ID delivers centralized account management, application access management, and enhanced identity protection. It supports role-based access control (RBAC) through service principals and service connections, including integration with Azure DevOps. It is used for managing access to services such as Azure Container Registry and provides integration with Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) for centralized identity and access management.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra ID is an authentication service used with Azure Service Bus for secure access.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra ID is an identity service integrated with multiple Azure services for authentication and authorization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc6c19c90a7ec75e7d95d807c1817fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062b3d27f8d0d9d1409bb3878692b58b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292724</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Defender For Container Registries">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Defender For Container Registries</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Defender for container registries provides vulnerability scanning for container images.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Defender for container registries provides security scanning for container images.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290963</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Containerization">
  <data key="d0">Containerization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Containerization is an abstraction layer for application code and dependencies, enabling portability and consistent execution across platforms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290963</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Composite SLO">
  <data key="d0">Composite SLO</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Composite SLO is a reliability metric calculated across user flows and deployment regions, with targets aligned to business requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Composite SLO defines combined service level objective targets for reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290963</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Content Delivery Network">
  <data key="d0">Content Delivery Network</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Content Delivery Network (CDN) minimizes network latency for distributed user bases through edge caching.&lt;SEP&gt;A Content Delivery Network (CDN) is a distributed content caching service that Azure Front Door's built-in cache can replace in many use cases.&lt;SEP&gt;A Content Delivery Network (CDN) serves static content; Azure Front Door's built-in cache can eliminate the need for a dedicated CDN in many use cases.&lt;SEP&gt;A CDN serves static content from edge nodes; Azure Front Door's built-in cache may eliminate the need for a dedicated CDN.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291996</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recovery Point Objectives">
  <data key="d0">Recovery Point Objectives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RPO defines the acceptable amount of data loss measured in time during a disaster.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290964</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recovery Time Objectives">
  <data key="d0">Recovery Time Objectives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RTO defines the acceptable downtime duration for recovering a service after a failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290964</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regional Pairs">
  <data key="d0">Regional Pairs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure regional pairs consist of two regions in a single geography, used to ensure business continuity and protection against data loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Regional pairs are Azure region pairings that benefit from serialized deployment (SDP) rollouts for planned maintenance and regional prioritization for unplanned maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290964</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Linux-Based Container Runtimes">
  <data key="d0">Linux-Based Container Runtimes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Linux-based container runtimes are recommended for containers due to lightweight images and frequent feature releases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290964</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Kubernetes Service">
  <data key="d0">Azure Kubernetes Service</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) is a managed Kubernetes container orchestration service provided by Microsoft Azure that enables quick cluster provisioning. It serves as an application hosting platform, notably used in baseline mission-critical architectures.

AKS offers advanced networking capabilities, including support for network policies, multiple networking models, Azure CNI static block allocation, and HTTP proxy support. It also provides features for identity management, reliability, custom certificate authority integration, and node pool configuration.

The service supports deployment strategies such as blue/green deployments through separate pod deployments on each node and service definition updates. AKS requires regular Kubernetes version updates and comes with architecture best practices guidance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68460066510727d2f753c0a61011f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab2911837499c055b346ca8d6a1cac17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20168b92f579ebd286ed6e8413a80537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50bf24a002558d213cd02700a64f5c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180631bfef52e56155ab10e925a1d9c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292769</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Container Apps">
  <data key="d0">Azure Container Apps</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Container Apps is an Azure platform for container management.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Container Apps is an Azure container hosting service.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Container Apps is an Azure service with architecture best practices covering security, performance, and cost optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Container Apps is a serverless container service with architecture best practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062b3d27f8d0d9d1409bb3878692b58b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292752</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Autoscaler">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Autoscaler</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster autoscaler automatically adjusts the number of agent nodes in response to resource constraints.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290964</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Horizontal Pod Autoscaler">
  <data key="d0">Horizontal Pod Autoscaler</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Horizontal pod autoscaler adjusts the number of pods in a deployment based on CPU utilization or other metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290965</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AKS Uptime SLA">
  <data key="d0">AKS Uptime SLA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">AKS Uptime SLA provides Kubernetes API endpoint availability guarantees for production clusters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290965</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Entra Workload ID">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Entra Workload ID</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Entra Workload ID enables managed identities at the pod level in AKS.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra Workload ID provides managed identities for Azure Kubernetes Service workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra Workload ID provides workload identity capabilities for AKS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290965</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual Nodes">
  <data key="d0">Virtual Nodes</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Virtual nodes provide extensive and rapid scale for high scale and burst scenarios in AKS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290965</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proximity Placement Groups">
  <data key="d0">Proximity Placement Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Proximity placement groups minimize internode latency when colocation latency is a concern in AKS deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Proximity placement groups reduce latency by co-locating AKS resources physically close together.&lt;SEP&gt;Proximity Placement Groups enable submillisecond latency between services by co-locating resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5df507c6d7ae6d803dce8c99d84eb9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292012</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AKS Security Baseline">
  <data key="d0">AKS Security Baseline</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">AKS security baseline provides configuration guidance for ensuring a suitable security posture for mission-critical scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290965</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kubernetes RBAC">
  <data key="d0">Kubernetes RBAC</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Kubernetes RBAC is used with Microsoft Entra ID for least privilege access control in AKS clusters.&lt;SEP&gt;Kubernetes RBAC (Role-Based Access Control) is used with Microsoft Entra ID to enforce least privilege access in AKS clusters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290965</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IaaS">
  <data key="d0">IaaS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) is a cloud computing model using virtual machines as the primary application hosting model.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b3d8041b90240539202a251be26880b7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290965</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PaaS">
  <data key="d0">PaaS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">PaaS (Platform as a Service) is a cloud service model that may have limitations for legacy or proprietary development software.&lt;SEP&gt;Platform as a Service (PaaS) is a cloud service model with lower operational costs and complexity compared to IaaS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b3d8041b90240539202a251be26880b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290965</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Marketplace">
  <data key="d0">Azure Marketplace</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Marketplace provides standard images for VM deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Marketplace provides standard images for virtual machines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b3d8041b90240539202a251be26880b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-682b99a48c23e193c28d8a4eae469e68</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mission-Critical Workloads">
  <data key="d0">Mission-Critical Workloads</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mission-Critical Workloads are applications and systems that require high reliability, high availability, and minimal downtime. On Azure, they are designed to maximize reliability so applications remain performant and available, with emphasis on disaster recovery and fast failure recovery.

The design methodology for Mission-Critical Workloads focuses on zero-downtime deployments, automation, and rapid failure recovery. Baseline architectures recommend following cloud-native patterns, including containerization and container orchestration. Specific data platform and architecture pattern considerations are also important, and the workloads may have varying business requirements that influence design decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b3d8041b90240539202a251be26880b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68460066510727d2f753c0a61011f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-390c92e4b952c987f9e0e7d0deeafa36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c445903885a1763cd6ad5557106d024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180631bfef52e56155ab10e925a1d9c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="North Star Architecture">
  <data key="d0">North Star Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The North Star architecture is the recommended cloud-native baseline pattern for mission-critical workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b3d8041b90240539202a251be26880b7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290966</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flexible Orchestration">
  <data key="d0">Flexible Orchestration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Flexible orchestration in scale sets protects against failures by automatically distributing VMs across fault domains.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b3d8041b90240539202a251be26880b7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290966</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chaos Experiments">
  <data key="d0">Chaos Experiments</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Chaos experiments inject application faults into VM components to observe and validate fault mitigation capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Chaos experiments involve injecting faults to validate application resilience, run alongside load tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b3d8041b90240539202a251be26880b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291481</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active/Passive">
  <data key="d0">Active/Passive</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Active/passive is a deployment strategy suitable for scenarios with lower reliability targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290966</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Safe Deployment Practice Framework">
  <data key="d0">Azure Safe Deployment Practice Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure SDP framework ensures code and configuration changes undergo phased rollout with health analysis across regional pairs.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Safe Deployment Practice (SDP) framework is a set of practices for advancing safe deployments on Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compute Decision Tree">
  <data key="d0">Compute Decision Tree</data>
