<node id="Azure Monitor">
  <data key="d0">Azure Monitor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Monitor is a comprehensive monitoring service provided by Microsoft Azure, enabled by default for all Azure subscriptions. It supports three core types of observability data: logs, metrics, and distributed traces, collecting operational data from a wide range of Azure resources.

Azure Monitor collects metrics, logs, and diagnostics across services such as Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS), Azure Cosmos DB, and Azure Cache for Redis. For AKS, it provides container insights with built-in Prometheus support. For Azure Cosmos DB, it gathers key metrics and diagnostic logs, including provisioned throughput, enabling near real-time operational insights and evaluation of database usage and sizing. It also evaluates health and key metrics for Azure Cache for Redis.

Azure Monitor provides an extensive alerting framework to detect, categorize, and respond to operational signals through Action Groups, supporting alerts, diagnostics, and observability across Azure resources. It integrates with Azure Dashboards for operational data visualization and supports Application Insights, with pricing based on data volume ingested and retention duration.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor is used to define alerts for unexpected key, certificate, and secret usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor provides health models with built-in alerting, visualizations, and easy integration for health modeling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73f080a578e1d5bcb7bab91a722b1c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee778ccfa3886c52f485cafeef0009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d35a819f81fdf6e061b2c836acac71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7620929405aff597a8fb7046b3e2aa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7255c274585b0f1f482e338bbc6c26aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50bf24a002558d213cd02700a64f5c07</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292780</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Policy">
  <data key="d0">Azure Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Policy is a governance service within the Azure Resource Manager control plane that enforces organizational standards, security, and reliability conventions across Azure resources. It supplements Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) by restricting actions that authorized users can perform, providing centralized governance safeguards and compliance enforcement.

Azure Policy offers a framework for enforcing and auditing security and reliability baselines, ensuring compliance with engineering criteria. It remediates or prohibits configuration deviations at configuration-time, automates management activities, and provides compliance reporting for Azure resources. It is used to enforce compliance for mission-critical workloads.

Azure Policy provides built-in policy definitions for governing specific Azure services. For example, it offers centralized governance safeguards for AKS clusters, controlling pod functions and establishing reliability and security baselines. It also provides built-in policy definitions for Azure Cosmos DB, such as disabling key-based metadata write access. Additionally, Azure Policy is used to ensure all regional resources route operational data to the correct Log Analytics workspace.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Policy is a governance service recommended for use with Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a324803e46dec295e5d9abb5a43f8a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c9347a4bec9630cfbf008260182d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc6c19c90a7ec75e7d95d807c1817fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062b3d27f8d0d9d1409bb3878692b58b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure CNI">
  <data key="d0">Azure CNI</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure CNI is a network plugin for AKS that enables Azure or Calico network policies for controlling traffic within clusters.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure CNI is a container networking interface for AKS that provides advanced networking capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure CNI is a network plugin for AKS network integration that supports a richer feature set.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure CNI is a robust and scalable network plugin recommended for most AKS scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;An advanced AKS networking model where nodes, pods, and services receive IP addresses from the same virtual network.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d7d8989458b7b6a8098b2c4cc007937</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global Traffic Routing">
  <data key="d0">Global Traffic Routing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Global traffic routing is a networking pattern for directing traffic across globally distributed deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Global traffic routing is the practice of distributing traffic across multiple active regional deployment stamps using global routing services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab841386ea8be41c85364b56959f5c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="App Service">
  <data key="d0">App Service</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure App Service is a cloud platform for hosting web applications with features like autoscaling, per-app scaling, and diagnostic logging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
