</node>
<node id="TCP Port Exhaustion">
  <data key="d0">TCP Port Exhaustion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TCP port exhaustion occurs when the sum of outbound connections from a given App Service worker exceeds capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;TCP port exhaustion occurs when outbound connections from a worker exceed capacity, depending on worker size.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290968</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Docker Hub">
  <data key="d0">Docker Hub</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Docker Hub is a public container registry that can lead to issues related to service availability, throttling, and data exfiltration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02</data>
