</node>
<node id="SNAT Port Exhaustion">
  <data key="d0">SNAT Port Exhaustion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SNAT port exhaustion is a common failure scenario in App Service when outbound connections to public IP addresses exceed available SNAT ports.&lt;SEP&gt;SNAT port exhaustion occurs when large numbers of outbound requests deplete available source NAT ports, preventing new outbound connections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Planned Maintenance">
  <data key="d0">Planned Maintenance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Planned Maintenance allows defining maintenance windows for AKS node and cluster update operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290970</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto-Upgrade Channels">
  <data key="d0">Auto-Upgrade Channels</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto-upgrade channels automatically upgrade AKS clusters to newer versions of Kubernetes or newer node images when available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777290970</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Core Architecture Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Core Architecture Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The core architecture pattern is a design approach for mission-critical applications consisting of global resources, regional stamp resources, and regional resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global Resources">
  <data key="d0">Global Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Global resources are long-living, globally distributed resources shared across regions, responsible for traffic distribution, permanent state storage, and monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regional Stamp Resources">
  <data key="d0">Regional Stamp Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Regional stamp resources are ephemeral, stateless resources deployed within a stamp that participate in completing business transactions and can be added or removed dynamically.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291014</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regional Resources">
  <data key="d0">Regional Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Regional resources are deployed in a region and outlive stamp resources, such as observability resources monitoring at the regional level.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291014</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="North Star Design Approach">
  <data key="d0">North Star Design Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The north star design approach is a recommended design methodology for starting mission-critical architecture design on Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291014</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Baseline Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Baseline Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The baseline architecture is a reference for mission-critical applications accessed over public endpoints without private network connectivity requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a68460066510727d2f753c0a61011f2f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291014</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Baseline With Network Controls">
  <data key="d0">Baseline With Network Controls</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An extension of the baseline architecture that provides strict network controls to prevent unauthorized public access to workload resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a68460066510727d2f753c0a61011f2f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291014</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Baseline In Azure Landing Zones">
  <data key="d0">Baseline In Azure Landing Zones</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An architecture for deploying mission-critical workloads in enterprise setups requiring integration with centralized shared services and on-premises connectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a68460066510727d2f753c0a61011f2f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291014</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Landing Zones">
  <data key="d0">Azure Landing Zones</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure landing zones provide a subscription model within enterprise management groups for deploying workloads with centralized shared services.&lt;SEP&gt;Standardized environments in Azure including platform and application landing zones for deploying workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure landing zones are a governed platform to help with onboarding workload teams, including platform landing zones and application landing zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a68460066510727d2f753c0a61011f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d07c7fd7e0ea2028615959913f9c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17e137434baf52b7c6f746bc411962c3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/workloads.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292842</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Well-Architected Assessment">
  <data key="d0">Well-Architected Assessment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Well-Architected Assessment is a review tool for self-assessing the readiness of mission-critical workloads in production, organized to check alignment to best practices for resiliency, reliability, and availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7092b7ad42e474e7a19995579b487a34</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-assessment.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291032</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mission-Critical Design Methodology">
  <data key="d0">Mission-Critical Design Methodology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The mission-critical design methodology provides foundational design principles for checking design choices of a workload's architecture and end-to-end operational approach.&lt;SEP&gt;A design methodology underpinned by five key design principles that serve as a compass for design decisions across critical design areas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7092b7ad42e474e7a19995579b487a34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-assessment.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cosmos DB SDK">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cosmos DB SDK</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Cosmos DB SDK provides built-in error handling, retry, and reliability capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB SDK provides client libraries with best practices and retry logic for application development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Connection Mode">
  <data key="d0">Direct Connection Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Direct connection mode optimizes network performance through direct TCP connectivity to backend Azure Cosmos DB nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Partitioning Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Partitioning Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A partitioning strategy optimizes data distribution across logical and physical partitions according to the data model.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CQRS">
  <data key="d0">CQRS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) is a pattern used to optimize data throughput.&lt;SEP&gt;CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) is an architectural pattern for asynchronous non-blocking messaging to load-level throughput.&lt;SEP&gt;Command and Query Responsibility Segregation is a pattern for load-leveling through asynchronous non-blocking messaging.&lt;SEP&gt;CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) is an architectural pattern for separating read and write operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-158c7610cc47ffd0b2e8ce56b6c723f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event Sourcing">
  <data key="d0">Event Sourcing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Event Sourcing is a persistence pattern used alongside CQRS to optimize throughput.&lt;SEP&gt;Event Sourcing is an architectural pattern used for asynchronous non-blocking messaging.&lt;SEP&gt;Event Sourcing is a pattern used alongside CQRS for asynchronous updates to Azure Cosmos DB.&lt;SEP&gt;Event Sourcing is an architectural pattern for storing state changes as a sequence of events.&lt;SEP&gt;Event Sourcing is an architecture pattern for capturing state changes as a sequence of events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73f080a578e1d5bcb7bab91a722b1c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-158c7610cc47ffd0b2e8ce56b6c723f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Security Baseline">
  <data key="d0">Azure Security Baseline</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Security Baseline provides control guidance for Azure Cosmos DB backup and recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Security Baseline provides security recommendations for Azure Cosmos DB including backup and recovery guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73f080a578e1d5bcb7bab91a722b1c8c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indexing">
  <data key="d0">Indexing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Indexing in Azure Cosmos DB is crucial for performance, using index exclusions to reduce RU/s and storage requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Indexing in Azure Cosmos DB allows efficient querying of data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Backups">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Backups</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous backups provide fine granularity of recovery points across the last 30 days for Azure Cosmos DB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic Failover">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Failover</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automatic failover is a feature for single write region configurations based on a defined failover priority considering all read region replicas.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic failover is recommended for single write region Azure Cosmos DB deployments to handle write region outages.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic failover ensures continuity of Azure Cosmos DB service during regional outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Region Write">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Region Write</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-region write is a data platform design pattern where changes to separate writeable replicas are synchronized and merged between all replicas with conflict resolution.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-region write is an Azure Cosmos DB configuration where a write replica exists in each deployment region to reduce latency and provide maximum redundancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Availability Zone Redundancy">
  <data key="d0">Availability Zone Redundancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Availability Zone redundancy ensures data replicas are placed across multiple availability zones to protect against zone failures within a region.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability Zone redundancy provides high availability support for Azure Cosmos DB across multiple availability zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paxos Consensus Protocol">
  <data key="d0">Paxos Consensus Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Paxos consensus protocol is applied to achieve quorum across replicas within a region in Azure Cosmos DB.&lt;SEP&gt;The Paxos consensus protocol is applied within the hub region to achieve quorum across replicas for conflict resolution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Last Write Wins">
  <data key="d0">Last Write Wins</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Last Write Wins is a standardized conflict resolution policy used in multi-region write contexts when the same data item is changed in two separate write-replicas.&lt;SEP&gt;Last Write Wins (LWW) is a conflict resolution policy that uses a time-synchronization clock protocol to resolve update conflicts by selecting the item with the highest timestamp value.&lt;SEP&gt;Last Write Wins (LWW) is the default conflict resolution policy in Azure Cosmos DB that uses a time-synchronization clock protocol to resolve conflicts by selecting the item with the highest timestamp value.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cosmos DB For NoSQL">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cosmos DB For NoSQL</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL is the first-party API providing the richest feature set, where new capabilities typically become available first.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL is an API that supports custom numerical properties for conflict resolution and custom resolution policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gateway Connectivity Mode">
  <data key="d0">Gateway Connectivity Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Gateway mode provides HTTPS connectivity to frontend gateway nodes for Azure Cosmos DB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Connectivity Mode">
  <data key="d0">Direct Connectivity Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Direct mode facilitates connectivity over TCP to backend Azure Cosmos DB replica nodes for improved performance with fewer network hops.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Application Architecture Guide">
  <data key="d0">Azure Application Architecture Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Application Architecture Guide provides additional data-platform guidance including decision trees and criteria for choosing data stores.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chaos Testing">
  <data key="d0">Chaos Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Chaos testing is used to test and validate backup, restore capabilities, and failover operations within continuous delivery processes.&lt;SEP&gt;A testing method that injects faults into an application under load to understand how it responds to failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Chaos testing injects artificial failures into the system to evaluate how it reacts and validate the effectiveness of resiliency measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Chaos testing is a testing approach used alongside load testing within CI/CD processes to observe and validate application health using the health model.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conflict Resolution">
  <data key="d0">Conflict Resolution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Conflict resolution addresses situations where the same data item is changed in two separate write replicas before either change can be replicated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service-Managed Encryption Keys">
  <data key="d0">Service-Managed Encryption Keys</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Service-managed encryption keys are recommended to reduce management complexity when applying encryption to data platforms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer-Managed Keys">
  <data key="d0">Customer-Managed Keys</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer-managed keys require appropriate key management procedures to ensure availability, backup, and rotation.&lt;SEP&gt;Customer-managed keys are encryption keys managed by the customer, used when clear regulatory requirements stipulate their use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Centralized Data Services">
  <data key="d0">Centralized Data Services</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Centralized data services (Central IT DBaaS) introduce operational bottlenecks that hinder agility and should be avoided in mission-critical or business-critical contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291343</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Data Store Decision Tree">
  <data key="d0">Azure Data Store Decision Tree</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Data Store Decision Tree is a reference guide within the Azure Application Architecture Guide for choosing data stores.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291343</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change Feed">
  <data key="d0">Change Feed</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Cosmos DB change feed provides a time-ordered feed of insert and update operations to data in a container, excluding deletes.&lt;SEP&gt;Change feed is a mechanism in Azure Cosmos DB that captures and propagates data record changes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Azure Cosmos DB change feed writes data to a separate storage facility and supports both continuous and periodic custom backups, though it doesn't yet reflect deletes.&lt;SEP&gt;Change feed provides a persistent record of changes to Azure Cosmos DB containers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291343</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soft-Delete Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Soft-Delete Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern where records are flagged as deleted (e.g., IsDeleted) rather than explicitly removed, allowing changes to propagate through the change feed before TTL-based automatic deletion.&lt;SEP&gt;A pattern using a boolean property and TTL to handle deletes in the Azure Cosmos DB change feed, required until full-fidelity updates are available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291344</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time-To-Live">
  <data key="d0">Time-To-Live</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time-To-Live (TTL) is a configuration for automatic expiration of data no longer required.&lt;SEP&gt;TTL is a setting that enables Azure Cosmos DB to automatically delete expired data after it has been reflected in the change feed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291344</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Analytical Store">
  <data key="d0">Analytical Store</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A column-format store in Azure Cosmos DB optimized for analytical queries, addressing ETL pipeline complexity and latency.&lt;SEP&gt;Analytical store is a column store for large-scale analytics on Azure Cosmos DB operational data.&lt;SEP&gt;Analytical Store is a feature of Azure Cosmos DB containers that can be enabled with analytical TTL configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522317310460c13e3a32323fc08f14d4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291344</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Periodic Backup Mode">
  <data key="d0">Periodic Backup Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Default backup mode with configurable intervals and retention periods, stored in Geo-Redundant Storage, requiring a support request for restore operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291345</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Backup Mode">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Backup Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Backup mode allowing point-in-time restore with one-second granularity within the last 30 days, with self-service restore capability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291345</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Geo-Redundant Storage">
  <data key="d0">Geo-Redundant Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
