<node id="Analytical Scenarios">
  <data key="d0">Analytical Scenarios</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Analytical scenarios drive additional value from data flows and require different data platform capabilities optimized for read queries and aggregations over large data volumes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transactional">
  <data key="d0">Transactional</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Transactional workloads process large volumes of individual transactions, optimized for near real-time CRUD queries with row-based storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enterprise Flash Tier">
  <data key="d0">Enterprise Flash Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Enterprise Flash tier of Azure Cache for Redis runs on a combination of RAM and flash non-volatile memory, enabling very large cache sizes up to 13TB with clustering.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AIOps">
  <data key="d0">AIOps</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">AIOps refers to application and operational analytical scenarios that form a crucial aspect of a highly reliable data platform.&lt;SEP&gt;AIOps refers to models that analyze and correlate application observability data from various environments.&lt;SEP&gt;AIOps applies AI methodologies in CI/CD pipelines to detect potential regressions or degradations and preemptively stop deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;AIOps (AI Operations) is a methodology applying machine learning to correlate and prioritize operational data, enabling detection, diagnosis, and prediction of system issues.&lt;SEP&gt;AIOps refers to the use of artificial intelligence for IT operations, involving ML model training on operational data for predictive and automated insights.&lt;SEP&gt;AIOps is the use of AI to continually improve operational procedures and triggers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ecbdde6d262012ebbdfa789102231a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11bac6534273a4d1656750c49ac2fcee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4678f659d2199619f053d40287ff2e4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7620929405aff597a8fb7046b3e2aa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a324803e46dec295e5d9abb5a43f8a29</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Single Server">
  <data key="d0">Single Server</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Single Server is a deployment option for Azure Database for PostgreSQL with 99.99% SLA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Failover Groups">
  <data key="d0">Auto Failover Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto Failover Groups replicate databases to a secondary server and allow transparent failover upon failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Failover Groups provide transparent failover to a secondary region with geo-replication for read optimization and database redundancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sharding">
  <data key="d0">Sharding</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sharding distributes data and processing across multiple identical structured databases by partitioning horizontally.&lt;SEP&gt;Sharding partitions relational databases based on different application and data contexts to maximize scalability, availability, and fault isolation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Business-Critical Service Tier">
  <data key="d0">Business-Critical Service Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Business-Critical service tier maximizes reliability and availability with critical resiliency capabilities for Azure SQL Database.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transparent Data Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Transparent Data Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Transparent Data Encryption (TDE) provides server-side at-rest encryption for Azure SQL Database.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zone-Redundant Deployment Model">
  <data key="d0">Zone-Redundant Deployment Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Zone-Redundant deployment model spreads Business Critical database replicas within the same region across Availability Zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reserved Capacity">
  <data key="d0">Reserved Capacity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reserved Capacity provides potential cost optimizations for Azure SQL Database and Azure Database for PostgreSQL compute costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Synapse Link">
  <data key="d0">Azure Synapse Link</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Synapse Link provides an analytical store whose data is not included in Azure Cosmos DB backups.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse Link enables direct querying of Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store from Azure Synapse, enabling no-ETL Hybrid Transactional-Analytical Processing (HTAP).&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse Link connects Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store to Azure Synapse for querying operational data without impacting transactional performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse Link enables connectivity between Azure Cosmos DB and Azure Synapse Analytics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-158c7610cc47ffd0b2e8ce56b6c723f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522317310460c13e3a32323fc08f14d4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Synapse Studio">
  <data key="d0">Azure Synapse Studio</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Synapse Studio provides a unified experience for ingestion and querying tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse Studio is the unified experience interface for Azure Synapse Analytics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-158c7610cc47ffd0b2e8ce56b6c723f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522317310460c13e3a32323fc08f14d4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Storage">
  <data key="d0">Azure Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Storage is used for 'cold' operations data for analytical purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Storage can be used as a target for custom backup implementations from Azure Cosmos DB.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Storage is a cloud storage service used as a data source and workspace storage for analytical scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Storage is an export destination for Log Analytics workspace data, supporting various redundancy levels including ZRS and GRS.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Storage in GRS configuration is recommended for long-term operational data storage exported from Log Analytics.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Storage in GRS configuration is used to host custom visuals and plugins for Grafana.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Storage is used for storing operational data, exported Log Analytics data, and prepared ML training data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-158c7610cc47ffd0b2e8ce56b6c723f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7620929405aff597a8fb7046b3e2aa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7255c274585b0f1f482e338bbc6c26aa</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291779</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Data Lake Gen2">
  <data key="d0">Azure Data Lake Gen2</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Data Lake Gen2 is a storage layer with hierarchical namespace, supported as an external store for Synapse queries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-158c7610cc47ffd0b2e8ce56b6c723f1</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CAP Theorem">
  <data key="d0">CAP Theorem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The CAP theorem expresses the trade-off between consistency and latency in distributed applications with multiple data replicas.&lt;SEP&gt;CAP theorem describes trade-offs between consistency, availability, and partition tolerance in distributed systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-158c7610cc47ffd0b2e8ce56b6c723f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SAGA">
  <data key="d0">SAGA</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SAGA is a design pattern applied to manage consistency and dependencies between different datastores in a microservice architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;SAGA is a design pattern used where dependencies between datastores exist in microservice architectures.&lt;SEP&gt;SAGA is a distributed transaction pattern referenced in the architecture documentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-158c7610cc47ffd0b2e8ce56b6c723f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PACELC Theorem">
  <data key="d0">PACELC Theorem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The PACELC theorem expresses the trade-off between consistency and latency in distributed applications with multiple data replicas.&lt;SEP&gt;PACELC theorem extends CAP theorem to describe trade-offs including latency and consistency in distributed systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-158c7610cc47ffd0b2e8ce56b6c723f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Data Factory">
  <data key="d0">Azure Data Factory</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Data Factory (ADF) is a batch-oriented orchestration service used to copy data from Azure Cosmos DB, supporting manual, schedule, tumbling window, and event-based triggers.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Data Factory provides connectors for Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL and MongoDB API with schedule, tumbling window, and event-based triggers.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Data Factory supports copy activity with various supported data stores and formats.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Data Factory provides ETL tools natively integrated with Azure Synapse for data extraction, transformation, loading, and orchestration.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Data Factory is an Azure data integration service.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522317310460c13e3a32323fc08f14d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d35a819f81fdf6e061b2c836acac71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4678f659d2199619f053d40287ff2e4a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Private Link">
  <data key="d0">Azure Private Link</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Private Link is supported by Azure Data Factory for high network security scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Private Link enables private endpoint connections for secure access to services like Azure Cosmos DB and Azure Data Factory.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Private Link provides dedicated access to Azure PaaS resources using private IP addresses and private network connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Private Link enables private connectivity to Azure services through private endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Private Link is referenced in networking guidance for Azure Virtual Desktop workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Private Link enables private connectivity to Azure services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65bdd00b5709152c19e73a1ad56171cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50bf24a002558d213cd02700a64f5c07</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292724</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change Feed Processor">
  <data key="d0">Change Feed Processor</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The change feed processor is a component that binds to the Azure Cosmos DB change feed to process items into storage.&lt;SEP&gt;Change feed processor is a library for consuming Azure Cosmos DB change feed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291352</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event Grid">
  <data key="d0">Event Grid</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Event Grid is supported by Azure Data Factory for event-based triggers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291352</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Single-Region Write">
  <data key="d0">Single-Region Write</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Single-region write is an Azure Cosmos DB configuration with globally distributed read replicas, offering 99.999% read SLA and 99.995% write SLA with Availability Zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291352</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ETL">
  <data key="d0">ETL</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Extract, Transform, and Load pipelines used to extract data into separate analytical platforms, consuming throughput and impacting transactional workload performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Extract, Transform, Load (ETL) is a traditional data processing approach that may not scale with deployment telemetry growth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ecbdde6d262012ebbdfa789102231a4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291483</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HTAP">
  <data key="d0">HTAP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hybrid Transactional-Analytical Processing enables querying transactional data for analytics in near real-time without ETL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto-Sync">
  <data key="d0">Auto-Sync</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The process where operational data changes are automatically synced to the Analytical Store, with latency usually less than two minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Synapse SQL Serverless Pools">
  <data key="d0">Azure Synapse SQL Serverless Pools</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">SQL Serverless pools in Azure Synapse that can query the Analytical Store through automatically updated views or SELECT/OPENROWSET commands.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Synapse Spark Pools">
  <data key="d0">Azure Synapse Spark Pools</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Spark pools in Azure Synapse that can query the Analytical Store through Spark tables or spark.read command, supporting dataframe operations and ML model training.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Request Unit">
  <data key="d0">Request Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Request Units (RUs) represent throughput consumed by operations on Azure Cosmos DB; analytical queries on transactional data can consume significant RUs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caching Layer">
  <data key="d0">Caching Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A caching layer is used to increase read throughput and improve user experience and end-to-end client response times.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microservice Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Microservice Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A microservice architecture allows individual application services to be built with distinct scenario-optimized datastores rather than depending on a single monolithic datastore.&lt;SEP&gt;Microservice architecture is a loosely coupled application design principle where individual services use distinct data stores and scenario-optimized data technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Apache Spark">
  <data key="d0">Apache Spark</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Apache Spark is an analytical runtime environment that may have integration restrictions to analyze polyglot data structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MACsec">
  <data key="d0">MACsec</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">MACsec (IEEE 802.1AE MAC) is a data-link encryption method used to secure all traffic moving between Azure datacenters on the Microsoft backbone network.&lt;SEP&gt;MACsec is a data-link layer encryption method used on underlying network hardware to secure data in-transit between Azure data centers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Key Vault">
  <data key="d0">Key Vault</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Key Vault is a secure location for managing encryption keys, supporting both server-side and client-side encryption scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Key Vault is an Azure secret management solution providing zone and regional redundancy, and integration with Microsoft Entra ID.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292095</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Variety">
  <data key="d0">Variety</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Variety refers to considerations around data models, data types, data relationships, and query models that affect data platform decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Variety is one of the Four Vs of Big Data, referring to the organization and format of data across structured, semi-structured, and unstructured formats.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Veracity">
  <data key="d0">Veracity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Veracity refers to validating the accuracy of data within an application, encompassing consistency, security, governance, and change management.&lt;SEP&gt;Veracity is one of the Four Vs of Big Data, referring to data provenance, curation, governance, and quality assurance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Volume">
  <data key="d0">Volume</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Volume refers to ensuring future data volumes do not exceed data platform capabilities, requiring capacity planning and monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Volume is one of the Four Vs of Big Data, referring to the size of the dataset and storage capacity requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Client-Side Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Client-Side Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Client-side encryption is an encryption approach implemented in the application layer where keys can be managed in Key Vault or another secure location.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Server-Side Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Server-Side Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Server-side encryption is an encryption approach implemented in the data layer using service-managed keys or customer-managed keys.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polyglot Storage">
  <data key="d0">Polyglot Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Polyglot storage refers to the capability of analytical datastores to support various types of data structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Custom Resolution Policies">
  <data key="d0">Custom Resolution Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Custom resolution policies allow application-defined semantics to reconcile conflicts using a registered merge stored procedure, available only with Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recovery Time Objective">
  <data key="d0">Recovery Time Objective</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The RTO provided by Azure Cosmos DB is approximately 10-15 minutes for regional failover, with a strategic direction to reduce to approximately 5 minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;Recovery Time Objective (RTO) defines the target time to recover an application after failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Recovery time objective (RTO) is a target metric for how quickly operations should be restored after a failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-390c92e4b952c987f9e0e7d0deeafa36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292723</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recovery Point Objective">
  <data key="d0">Recovery Point Objective</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RPO is configurable via consistency levels, with a minimum of 0 for strong consistency with single-write region.&lt;SEP&gt;Recovery Point Objective (RPO) defines the acceptable amount of data loss measured in time.&lt;SEP&gt;Recovery point objective (RPO) defines the tolerance for data loss in disaster recovery scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-390c92e4b952c987f9e0e7d0deeafa36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292724</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hub Region">
  <data key="d0">Hub Region</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The hub region is the primary region in Azure Cosmos DB's multi-region write configuration responsible for all conflict resolutions, determined by the first region configured.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Message Buffer">
  <data key="d0">Message Buffer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The message buffer stores write conflicts within the hub region to provide load leveling and redundancy, capable of storing a few minutes worth of write updates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consistency Levels">
  <data key="d0">Consistency Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Consistency levels in Azure Cosmos DB are configurable settings that affect RPO, RTO, data durability, and throughput trade-offs, with five levels available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Throughput">
  <data key="d0">Standard Throughput</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard throughput allocates fixed resources to guarantee a specified RU/s value, billed hourly for provisioned throughput.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Traffic Manager">
  <data key="d0">Azure Traffic Manager</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Traffic Manager controls routing to specific gateway rings in Azure SQL Database.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Traffic Manager is a globally distributed routing service with built-in multi-region redundancy and availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Traffic Manager is a DNS redirection service that routes traffic based on configured rules without processing request payloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Traffic Manager is a global routing service for non-HTTP/S scenarios, used as a replacement to Azure Front Door with different design considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Traffic Manager is a DNS-based traffic load balancing service.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Traffic Manager is an Azure service with enhanced health probing and failover practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Traffic Manager is a DNS-based traffic load balancer with architecture best practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d7d8989458b7b6a8098b2c4cc007937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab2911837499c055b346ca8d6a1cac17</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292768</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dedicated Gateway">
  <data key="d0">Dedicated Gateway</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dedicated Gateway is a connection mode feature of Azure Cosmos DB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consistency Level">
  <data key="d0">Consistency Level</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Consistency level defines the data consistency guarantees offered by Azure Cosmos DB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Role-Based Access Control">
  <data key="d0">Role-Based Access Control</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">RBAC provides built-in and custom roles for controlling access to Azure Cosmos DB resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Role-based access control is used to delegate incremental firewall policies to application security teams for policy autonomy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5df507c6d7ae6d803dce8c99d84eb9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Periodic Backup">
  <data key="d0">Periodic Backup</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Periodic backup provides scheduled backup with zone-redundant or locally-redundant storage options, restored via support request.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Backup">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Backup</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous backup enables point-in-time restore via Azure portal or ARM templates, with some limitations and additional storage cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Function">
  <data key="d0">Azure Function</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Function can be triggered by Azure Cosmos DB change feed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Partition Key">
  <data key="d0">Partition Key</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Partition key selection is critical for optimal performance and data distribution in Azure Cosmos DB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARM Template">
  <data key="d0">ARM Template</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">ARM Template is a method for configuring Azure Cosmos DB settings including RBAC, restore, and infrastructure as code deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stored Procedures">
  <data key="d0">Stored Procedures</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stored procedures are server-side programmable logic that can be deployed in Azure Cosmos DB SQL database containers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Triggers">
  <data key="d0">Triggers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Triggers are server-side logic executed before or after operations on Azure Cosmos DB containers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UDFs">
  <data key="d0">UDFs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">User-defined functions (UDFs) are custom functions that can be created in Azure Cosmos DB SQL database containers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MongoDB API">
  <data key="d0">MongoDB API</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MongoDB API is an Azure Cosmos DB API that enables MongoDB-compatible access, supported by Azure Data Factory connector.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conflict Resolution Policies">
  <data key="d0">Conflict Resolution Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Conflict resolution policies handle update conflicts (insert, replace, delete) in Azure Cosmos DB multi-region writes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b4894fcd598b00b3316bd49945a116d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Column Store">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Column Store</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Column Store is a data store component that separates transactional and analytical data in Azure Cosmos DB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-522317310460c13e3a32323fc08f14d4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spark Dataframe">
  <data key="d0">Spark Dataframe</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Spark dataframe is used to load and query data from the analytical store.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-522317310460c13e3a32323fc08f14d4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synapse Spark">
  <data key="d0">Synapse Spark</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Synapse Spark is a component of Azure Synapse Analytics used for querying data including Log Analytics exported data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-522317310460c13e3a32323fc08f14d4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Tiering">
  <data key="d0">Data Tiering</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data tiering classifies datasets into 'hot', 'warm', and 'cold' tiers based on usage and criticality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Region Data Platform">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Region Data Platform</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A multi-region data platform distributes replicas across regions for maximum reliability, availability, and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caching">
  <data key="d0">Caching</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Caching is implemented for 'hot' data scenarios to minimize response times, with policies for expiration and housekeeping.&lt;SEP&gt;Caching of static content at the edge to speed up client load times, reduce backend load, and lower costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Four Vs Of Big Data">
  <data key="d0">Four Vs Of Big Data</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Four Vs of Big Data is a framework comprising Volume, Velocity, Variety, and Veracity characteristics used to design highly available data platforms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time To Live">
  <data key="d0">Time To Live</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time to Live (TTL) is a feature that manages data growth by automatically deleting records after an elapsed time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Active Geographical Distribution">
  <data key="d0">Active-Active Geographical Distribution</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-active geographical distribution is a design pattern for deploying applications across multiple regions simultaneously, introducing data consistency challenges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Velocity">
  <data key="d0">Velocity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Velocity is one of the Four Vs of Big Data, referring to the speed at which data is processed as batches or continuous streams.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Penetration Testing">
  <data key="d0">Penetration Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Penetration testing ensures that an application and its environment meet requirements of an expected security posture by identifying security vulnerabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Penetration testing ensures that an application and its environment meet security posture requirements by identifying security vulnerabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Penetration testing is a procedure used to verify threat mitigation against potential threats.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75881c2e5d7a1909b7080e2819bc0413</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Common Vulnerabilities And Exposures">
  <data key="d0">Common Vulnerabilities And Exposures</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CVE is a system for identifying known security vulnerabilities in software supply chains and package dependencies.&lt;SEP&gt;CVEs are tracked within utilized package dependencies as part of securing the software supply chain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292364</data>
