</node>
<node id="Development Environments">
  <data key="d0">Development Environments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Development environments are short-lived environments created as required for parallel feature development, with lower requirements for reliability, capacity, and security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291484</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Test Or Staging Environments">
  <data key="d0">Test Or Staging Environments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Test or staging environments are short-lived environments used for testing and validation before production deployment, reflecting production capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291485</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Validation And Testing">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Validation And Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous validation and testing is a practice describing appropriate test cycles for mission-critical workloads to ensure bug-free deployment to production.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous validation and testing is a critical activity for validating health of application code and infrastructure across reliability, performance, availability, security, quality, and scale.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous validation and testing is a performance efficiency principle.&lt;SEP&gt;Automated testing within CI/CD processes including load testing and chaos experimentation to validate thresholds and identify risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb446ff77685d5a057445825bab9dcd5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blue-Green Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Blue-Green Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Blue-green deployment is a deployment strategy where traffic is transitioned between two environments (blue and green), with the inactive environment decommissioned after transition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291485</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unit Testing">
  <data key="d0">Unit Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Unit testing confirms that application business logic works as expected and validates the overall effect of code changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291485</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smoke Testing">
  <data key="d0">Smoke Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Smoke testing identifies whether infrastructure and application components are available and function as expected, typically testing a single virtual user session.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291485</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UI Testing">
  <data key="d0">UI Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">UI testing validates that application user interfaces are deployed and that user interface interactions function as expected using UI automation tools to mimic realistic user scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291485</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Testing">
  <data key="d0">Performance Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance testing combines aspects of load and stress testing to validate performance under load and establish benchmark behaviors.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance testing is a key capability used to define and continually evaluate application health by understanding component operational characteristics under steady state production load.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subscription-Scoped Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Subscription-Scoped Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subscription-scoped deployment involves using multiple Azure subscriptions as scale units to avoid single subscription scale limits for mission-critical applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291485</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design Methodology">
  <data key="d0">Design Methodology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design methodology for mission-critical applications on Azure that emphasizes reliability objectives, automation, zero-downtime deployments, fast failure detection, and evolving with Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Design methodology is the recommended starting point for reviewing mission-critical application scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;A systematic approach that outlines rationale and recurring themes across technical and operational areas to help define requirements and design strategies for mission-critical workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-390c92e4b952c987f9e0e7d0deeafa36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c80c2e3daca343330a4078ee96575423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292195</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Level Objectives">
  <data key="d0">Service Level Objectives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Service Level Objectives (SLOs) define availability targets such as 99.9% or 99.999% availability for workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-390c92e4b952c987f9e0e7d0deeafa36</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zero-Downtime Deployments">
  <data key="d0">Zero-Downtime Deployments</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Zero-downtime deployments ensure users experience no disruption during changes, requiring rigorous testing and end-to-end automation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-390c92e4b952c987f9e0e7d0deeafa36</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Well-Architected Framework">
  <data key="d0">Well-Architected Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Well-Architected Framework is a Microsoft framework that provides best practices for designing, building, and operating cloud workloads. It consists of five pillars: Reliability, Security, Cost Optimization, Operational Excellence, and Performance Efficiency. These pillars serve as the technical foundation for building highly reliable solutions and guiding architectural best practices for Azure services, though the framework's principles, checklists, and guides are applicable to all cloud platforms and most workload types, including mission-critical workloads.

The framework offers design principles, checklists, tradeoffs, and workload guides that provide clarity for design and implementation by offering rationalizations for architectural decisions. It includes a maturity model with a structured curriculum and milestones for workload teams to follow. Continuous improvement is a recurring theme across all pillars.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-390c92e4b952c987f9e0e7d0deeafa36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5505883d3947b5183a0241244e460f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d7ba45bf48a024a996731f69cab5301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20168b92f579ebd286ed6e8413a80537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50bf24a002558d213cd02700a64f5c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-830fe53dca8ce291e75061d94230f1bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17e137434baf52b7c6f746bc411962c3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/what-is-well-architected-framework.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/workloads.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="End-To-End Automation">
  <data key="d0">End-To-End Automation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">End-to-end automation is a strategy spanning deployment and ongoing management, emphasizing consistency, repeatability, and resilience through automation-first principles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-390c92e4b952c987f9e0e7d0deeafa36</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md</data>
