<node id="Health Modeling">
  <data key="d0">Health Modeling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A design guide about health modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;Health modeling is a process of defining a robust health model by mapping quantified application health states through observability and operational constructs to maximize reliability of mission-critical workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Health modeling improves workload reliability by quantifying application health and building custom health models combining business context with monitoring data.&lt;SEP&gt;Health modeling is a design guide practice for monitoring and assessing the health of workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6d5fef3c980e677376967817f32d9dad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5edbb96d862689f4578c3260e170ce09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180631bfef52e56155ab10e925a1d9c4</data>
