<node id="Disaster Recovery">
  <data key="d0">Disaster Recovery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Planning and practice drills essential for recovering from unplanned downtime events.&lt;SEP&gt;Disaster recovery involves technical mitigations and processes for business continuity, distinguished from routine incident management.&lt;SEP&gt;Strategies and plans for recovering from disruptions including multi-region deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-75881c2e5d7a1909b7080e2819bc0413&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e1b9f43effe85bb4f106ab0a823c7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180631bfef52e56155ab10e925a1d9c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292775</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Cost Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cost Optimization is one of the five pillars of the Azure Well-Architected Framework, focused on delivering sufficient return on investment while reducing waste. It encompasses cost modeling, budgets, rate optimization, dynamic scaling, and resource utilization, balancing reliability investments against financial costs and avoiding over-engineering beyond business requirements.

As a pillar, Cost Optimization includes its own design principles, checklists, tradeoffs, and a maturity model. It is also identified as one of the five mission-critical design principles, emphasizing budgeting and efficient resource management across cloud architectures.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the five architectural pillars of the Azure Well-Architected Framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-75881c2e5d7a1909b7080e2819bc0413&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174d80fe9b4a084487aca3f0463ecf9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-387611e470f83bbe5d875c098db01fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5505883d3947b5183a0241244e460f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3794cb2593672d7e205ce2c3021b80ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c445903885a1763cd6ad5557106d024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062b3d27f8d0d9d1409bb3878692b58b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4e1326f308873031b3e530e46d8478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d07c7fd7e0ea2028615959913f9c73</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/pillars.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/what-is-well-architected-framework.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/workloads.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security">
  <data key="d0">Security</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security is one of the five pillars of the Azure Well-Architected Framework, serving as a mission-critical design principle area. It focuses on protecting applications and workloads against threats that could compromise reliability, confidentiality, integrity, and availability.

Security encompasses threat modeling, endpoint protection, code vulnerability protection, data encryption, least privilege automation, data protection, threat detection, and mitigation. It addresses how workloads mitigate specific threats such as DDoS attacks, bearing on overall reliability. As a pillar of the Well-Architected Framework, Security includes design principles, checklists, and tradeoffs to guide architectural decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Security is one of the five pillars of the Azure Well-Architected Framework.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the five pillars of the Azure Well-Architected Framework with its own maturity model.&lt;SEP&gt;Security is a pillar covering networking, connectivity, and segmentation strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the five architectural pillars of the Azure Well-Architected Framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-75881c2e5d7a1909b7080e2819bc0413&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c80c2e3daca343330a4078ee96575423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174d80fe9b4a084487aca3f0463ecf9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-387611e470f83bbe5d875c098db01fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5505883d3947b5183a0241244e460f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3794cb2593672d7e205ce2c3021b80ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c445903885a1763cd6ad5557106d024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4e1326f308873031b3e530e46d8478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d07c7fd7e0ea2028615959913f9c73</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/pillars.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/what-is-well-architected-framework.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/workloads.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292840</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SlowLoris">
  <data key="d0">SlowLoris</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SlowLoris is an example of a DDoS attack vector mentioned as a common threat against network endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;SlowLoris is an attack vector that can impact application reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-75881c2e5d7a1909b7080e2819bc0413&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505</data>
