  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Least Privilege">
  <data key="d0">Least Privilege</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Least privilege is a security principle applied across application and control plane to protect against data exfiltration and malicious actors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-75881c2e5d7a1909b7080e2819bc0413</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reliability">
  <data key="d0">Reliability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reliability is one of the five pillars of the Azure Well-Architected Framework, focused on resiliency, availability, and recoverability. It serves as the primary focus pillar for mission-critical workloads within the framework.

Reliability encompasses a broad set of design principles and practices, including active/active design, fault isolation, application health monitoring, automation, self-healing, and complexity avoidance. It covers key areas such as redundancy, scaling strategy, disaster recovery, failure mode analysis, self-preservation, resilience patterns, and testing strategies.

As a framework pillar, Reliability includes its own design principles, checklists, tradeoffs, and maturity model to guide architects in building robust and dependable solutions on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the five architectural pillars of the Azure Well-Architected Framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c80c2e3daca343330a4078ee96575423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174d80fe9b4a084487aca3f0463ecf9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-387611e470f83bbe5d875c098db01fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5505883d3947b5183a0241244e460f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3794cb2593672d7e205ce2c3021b80ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c445903885a1763cd6ad5557106d024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062b3d27f8d0d9d1409bb3878692b58b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4e1326f308873031b3e530e46d8478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180631bfef52e56155ab10e925a1d9c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d07c7fd7e0ea2028615959913f9c73</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/pillars.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/what-is-well-architected-framework.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/workloads.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292840</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Efficiency">
  <data key="d0">Performance Efficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance Efficiency is one of the five pillars of the Azure Well-Architected Framework, focused on scalability and accomplishing purpose within acceptable timeframes. It emphasizes maintaining a consistent level of application service and performance relative to a known healthy state.

The pillar's design principles include scale-out design, automation for hyperscale, continuous validation and testing, managed compute services, baseline performance identification, and capacity modeling. It encompasses load testing as a key practice for ensuring scalable and performant systems.

Performance Efficiency includes its own maturity model, design principles, checklists, and tradeoffs to guide architects in building efficient cloud solutions on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the five architectural pillars of the Azure Well-Architected Framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c80c2e3daca343330a4078ee96575423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174d80fe9b4a084487aca3f0463ecf9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-387611e470f83bbe5d875c098db01fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5505883d3947b5183a0241244e460f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3794cb2593672d7e205ce2c3021b80ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c445903885a1763cd6ad5557106d024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4e1326f308873031b3e530e46d8478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d07c7fd7e0ea2028615959913f9c73</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/pillars.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/what-is-well-architected-framework.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/workloads.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operational Excellence">
  <data key="d0">Operational Excellence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Operational Excellence is one of the five pillars of the Azure Well-Architected Framework, focused on responsible development and operations. It encompasses DevOps practices, holistic observability, automation, and loosely coupled component design with automated build and release processes.

The pillar covers a broad range of concerns including operations standardization, monitoring, safe deployment practices, incident response, risk management, and development formalization. It provides design principles, checklists, tradeoffs, and design patterns to guide practitioners. Operational Excellence also has its own maturity model within the framework.

Operational Excellence directly impacts application availability by addressing how a workload responds to operational issues. More broadly, it is oriented toward achieving high performance and efficiency in operations through standardized practices and continuous improvement.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the five architectural pillars of the Azure Well-Architected Framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c80c2e3daca343330a4078ee96575423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174d80fe9b4a084487aca3f0463ecf9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-387611e470f83bbe5d875c098db01fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5505883d3947b5183a0241244e460f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3794cb2593672d7e205ce2c3021b80ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c445903885a1763cd6ad5557106d024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e1b9f43effe85bb4f106ab0a823c7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062b3d27f8d0d9d1409bb3878692b58b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df4a711d3025404c202424f3f750081c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4e1326f308873031b3e530e46d8478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180631bfef52e56155ab10e925a1d9c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d07c7fd7e0ea2028615959913f9c73</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/pillars.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/what-is-well-architected-framework.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/workloads.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292841</data>
