  <data key="d5">1777291784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dedicated Clusters">
  <data key="d0">Dedicated Clusters</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dedicated Clusters are a deployment option enabling Availability Zones for protection from zone failures, requiring a minimum daily data ingest commitment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7255c274585b0f1f482e338bbc6c26aa</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Micro-Segmentation">
  <data key="d0">Micro-Segmentation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A network security design pattern used to isolate and secure individual application workloads based on a Zero Trust model.&lt;SEP&gt;Micro-segmentation is an advanced zero-trust network implementation technique employing distributed ingress/egress micro-perimeters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc6c19c90a7ec75e7d95d807c1817fcf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Security Groups">
  <data key="d0">Network Security Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NSGs provide IP ACL-based security at subnet or network interface level for micro-segmentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Security Groups are used to micro-segment application traffic and enforce security rules on subnets.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Security Groups are used to filter and restrict network traffic and access between subnets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c9347a4bec9630cfbf008260182d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zero Trust">
  <data key="d0">Zero Trust</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A security model that limits network traffic between workloads based on strict access policies.&lt;SEP&gt;Zero Trust is a Microsoft security model that provides a proactive and integrated approach to applying security across all layers of an application, centered on eliminating trust and enforcing verification.&lt;SEP&gt;Zero Trust is a security model that assumes a breached state and verifies each request as though it originates from an uncontrolled network.&lt;SEP&gt;Zero Trust is a security model promoted by Microsoft based on guiding principles for securing systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Zero Trust is a security model with guiding principles referenced for mission-critical workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c9347a4bec9630cfbf008260182d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc6c19c90a7ec75e7d95d807c1817fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65bdd00b5709152c19e73a1ad56171cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kubenet">
  <data key="d0">Kubenet</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Kubenet is a network plugin for AKS suitable for scenarios with limited available IP addresses.&lt;SEP&gt;Kubenet is a lightweight network plugin recommended for scenarios with limited IP address ranges.&lt;SEP&gt;A lightweight AKS networking model where pods exist in a virtual overlay network and traffic between nodes is routed through kube-proxy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d7d8989458b7b6a8098b2c4cc007937</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Policies">
  <data key="d0">Network Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Kubernetes specification defining access policies for communication between pods using label selectors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Node Pools">
  <data key="d0">Node Pools</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Node pools in AKS allow separating workloads using nodes with different hardware and software characteristics, but do not provide network-level isolation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Express Route">
  <data key="d0">Express Route</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Express Route is an Azure service providing secure and scalable on-premises network connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Express Route is a connectivity method for connecting Azure regions, on-premises networks, and other cloud platforms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5df507c6d7ae6d803dce8c99d84eb9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Bastion">
  <data key="d0">Azure Bastion</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Bastion is a fully platform-managed PaaS service providing secure RDP/SSH connectivity to Azure VMs without requiring public IP addresses.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Bastion provides proxied private connections to access the data plane of Azure resources or perform management operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Bastion provides secure remote connectivity to virtual machines.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Bastion provides secure access to Azure Virtual Machines and administrative tasks on Azure PaaS over the Internet.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Bastion is an Azure service providing secure remote access to virtual machines.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Bastion is a service for secure remote access to Virtual Machines without exposing them to public internet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d7d8989458b7b6a8098b2c4cc007937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c9347a4bec9630cfbf008260182d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65bdd00b5709152c19e73a1ad56171cd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure NAT Gateway">
  <data key="d0">Azure NAT Gateway</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure NAT Gateway is a scalable NAT solution supporting 64,000 connections per assigned outbound IP address, with up to 16 IP addresses per gateway.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure NAT Gateway provides outbound network connectivity for virtual networks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d7d8989458b7b6a8098b2c4cc007937</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Firewall">
  <data key="d0">Azure Firewall</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Firewall is a network security service in Azure that provides capabilities to secure network egress, control and inspect outbound internet traffic, and filter and restrict egress traffic for resources such as Virtual Machines and Azure Kubernetes Service. It can be deployed as dedicated or centrally shared instances and requires a dedicated subnet within a virtual network.

Azure Firewall offers features including Resource Health monitoring, explicit proxy configuration, customer-controlled maintenance, change tracking, and FQDN filtering in DNAT rules. Microsoft provides architecture best practices and guidance for configuring and operating Azure Firewall effectively.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d7d8989458b7b6a8098b2c4cc007937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5df507c6d7ae6d803dce8c99d84eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c9347a4bec9630cfbf008260182d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab2911837499c055b346ca8d6a1cac17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50bf24a002558d213cd02700a64f5c07</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Load Balancer">
  <data key="d0">Azure Load Balancer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Load Balancer is an Azure service providing direct internet outbound connectivity for virtual machines or compute instances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RFC 1918">
  <data key="d0">RFC 1918</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RFC 1918 defines address allocation for private internet IP addresses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Address Translation">
  <data key="d0">Network Address Translation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">NAT is a compute operation in the networking stack that translates addresses when traffic from a virtual network travels to the Internet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blue-Green Deployments">
  <data key="d0">Blue-Green Deployments</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Blue-green deployments are a deployment strategy using parallel subnets to facilitate updated regional deployment stamps within virtual networks.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue-green deployments are a deployment strategy using parallel subnets to facilitate updated regional deployment stamps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291991</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual Network Peering">
  <data key="d0">Virtual Network Peering</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Virtual network peering is a networking resource that creates complications if application virtual networks are treated as ephemeral.&lt;SEP&gt;Virtual network peering connects networks within a region and across different regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5df507c6d7ae6d803dce8c99d84eb9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VPN">
  <data key="d0">VPN</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">VPN serves as a failover connectivity mechanism providing additional redundancy alongside ExpressRoute.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Web Application Firewall">
  <data key="d0">Azure Web Application Firewall</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF) can be used on Azure Front Door for traffic inspection and security.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF) can be deployed on Azure Front Door at network edge locations to inspect every incoming request.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure DDoS Protection Basic">
  <data key="d0">Azure DDoS Protection Basic</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure DDoS Protection Basic provides built-in DDoS attack protection for Azure Front Door application endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure DDoS Protection Basic is integrated into Azure Front Door by default, providing always-on traffic monitoring and real-time mitigation against Layer 3/4 and Layer 7 attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ee1b46c13062b2f84bc4bd8740f6c3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291994</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure DDoS Standard">
  <data key="d0">Azure DDoS Standard</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure DDoS Standard provides additional advanced protection and detection capabilities as an added layer to Azure Front Door.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291994</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Front Door Premium">
  <data key="d0">Azure Front Door Premium</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Front Door Premium supports private endpoints enabling direct internet-to-VNet traffic flow without public IPs.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Front Door Premium can route directly from edge nodes to private application endpoints.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291995</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Gateway WAF">
  <data key="d0">Application Gateway WAF</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Application Gateway WAF provides a slightly different feature set from Front Door WAF but supports built-in and custom rules in detection or prevention mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291996</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Standard Load Balancer">
  <data key="d0">Azure Standard Load Balancer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Standard Load Balancer provides cross-region routing capabilities for managing global traffic.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Standard Load Balancer with cross-region capability is available in preview and not recommended for mission-critical workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Standard Load Balancer is a load balancing service backed by an SLA, unlike the Basic SKU.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Standard Load Balancer is an Azure SKU for internal traffic distribution providing 99.99% SLA across Availability Zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ee1b46c13062b2f84bc4bd8740f6c3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Session Affinity">
  <data key="d0">Session Affinity</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Session Affinity uses client-side cookies to route subsequent requests to the same backend as the first request.&lt;SEP&gt;Session Affinity is a routing feature that can negatively impact traffic distribution balance and should not be enabled unless required by the application.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Application Gateway">
  <data key="d0">Azure Application Gateway</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Application Gateway provides WAF capabilities within each regional deployment stamp.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Application Gateway is a regional Azure service that provides WAF capabilities for ingress traffic.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Application Gateway v2 is a web traffic load balancer with architecture best practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ee1b46c13062b2f84bc4bd8740f6c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233362b748b88ddd9ff57f063cacd0c2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292747</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure DDoS Network Protection">
  <data key="d0">Azure DDoS Network Protection</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure DDoS Network Protection helps protect public endpoints hosted within application virtual networks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777291999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure CDN">
  <data key="d0">Azure CDN</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure CDN supports Azure WAF enablement, currently in public preview.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Content Delivery Network service for establishing content delivery networks, more cost effective than Azure Front Door but with fewer advanced routing and WAF capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ee1b46c13062b2f84bc4bd8740f6c3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="WAF">
  <data key="d0">WAF</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Web Application Firewall provides security capabilities to block attacks on publicly exposed endpoints, configurable in Prevention or Detection mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual Network Integration">
  <data key="d0">Virtual Network Integration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Network-level integration approach for mission-critical applications, supporting public or private connectivity configurations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TLS">
  <data key="d0">TLS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TLS (Transport Layer Security) connections are enabled via Azure Front Door managed certificate service, removing the need to manage certificate lifecycles.&lt;SEP&gt;TLS (Transport Layer Security) is a protocol used for encrypted connections, with TLS offloading occurring before traffic reaches application backends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Akamai">
  <data key="d0">Akamai</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Akamai is a third-party CDN provider that can integrate with Azure CDN for content delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292003</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Verizon">
  <data key="d0">Verizon</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Verizon is a third-party CDN provider that can integrate with Azure CDN for content delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292003</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Policy">
  <data key="d0">Network Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Network Policy is a Kubernetes feature used to define ingress and egress traffic rules between pods in a cluster.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d7d8989458b7b6a8098b2c4cc007937</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure DNS">
  <data key="d0">Azure DNS</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure DNS is a shared foundational service that serves as a global platform dependency for almost all Azure services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775</data>
