</node>
<node id="RTO/RPO">
  <data key="d0">RTO/RPO</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RTO (Recovery Time Objective) and RPO (Recovery Point Objective) are data retention and recovery requirements that backup and restore strategies should align with.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777292096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deployment-Time Retrieval">
  <data key="d0">Deployment-Time Retrieval</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Deployment-time retrieval is a secret management approach where secrets are read from the secret store and injected into the application at deployment time, removing direct runtime dependencies on the secret store.&lt;SEP&gt;A secret retrieval approach where secrets are injected at deployment time, requiring full redeployment for updates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce</data>
